  "id": "balance-control",
  "term": "balance control",
  "definition": "Balance control is the neuromechanical ability to keep the body stable and accurately regulate posture during standing and movement. In this context, it is evaluated through patterns of postural stability, often using center-of-pressure measures to detect differences in how people regulate balance.",
